CloudBurrow patch 1 of 2 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061; the bug: #1065, #1075).

The bug: BigQuery's API carries a BYTES value as base64 (a streamed row, a
JSON or CSV load, a query's rows written to a destination table), but
Repository.AddTableData bound that string as it was, and the engine casts a
string to BYTES as the string's own bytes, so it stored the base64 text: a
value written as "/w==" (the byte 0xff) read back as the bytes "/w==". The
patch decodes each string in a BYTES position, at the top level, in a
REPEATED column and in a RECORD, before it is bound (a JSON load now hands
AddTableData each column's whole field, mode and subfields too, which it
dropped); a []byte (the Storage Write API's) is bound as before, and a string
that is not base64 fails the write. bytes_test.go fails without the patch and passes with it.

